#. default-sha256: 3274b8abddcdfc1b94a0d7e6c1e08fc439dba0c2772f9885726a42d54193fd37
msgctxt "search2:search2_C396F1A2_065E_47D4_A632_E6625AAA9A30"
msgid "⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫“You’re just as guilty as any of us.”"
msgstr "⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫“Você é tão culpado quanto qualquer um de nós.”"

#: search2:search2_EA31D2A2_E164_4FEE_8062_FAEFDCADAAE4
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 3952405af217d72afbf8515afda784bc6a84c06a1f08877e8463c0ef5ff86907
#. default-sha256: bbabfe183664b7ebff37f5f90d89d96ab58062d631f2320df054f770338c36a7
msgctxt "search2:search2_EA31D2A2_E164_4FEE_8062_FAEFDCADAAE4"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Not only did they not mourn my death—they argued over whose fault it was. ⟪k:2⟫There "
"was no regret—no remorse.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫The young man muttered absentmindedly, ⟪k:6⟫“I... I never "
"⟪k:7⟫wanted⟪k:8⟫ her to die...”⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫What did his ⟪k:12⟫intentions⟪k:13⟫ matter, "
"though? ⟪k:14⟫It was his betrayal that had ultimately tethered me to this mansion.⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫"
"⟪k:17⟫⟪k:18⟫But the fact that they didn’t grieve my death... ⟪k:19⟫and instead squabbled amongst "
"themselves like filthy rats... ⟪k:20⟫was the final straw."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Eles não apenas não lamentaram minha morte—como discutiram sobre de quem era a culpa. "
"⟪k:2⟫Não houve arrependimento—nenhum remorso.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫O jovem murmurou distraído, "
"⟪k:6⟫“Eu... eu nunca ⟪k:7⟫quis⟪k:8⟫ que ela morresse...”⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫O que importava suas "
"⟪k:12⟫intenções⟪k:13⟫, no entanto? ⟪k:14⟫Por fim, foi a traição dele que me prendeu a esta mansão."
"⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫⟪k:17⟫⟪k:18⟫Mas o fato de que eles não lamentaram minha morte... ⟪k:19⟫e, em vez "
"disso, brigaram entre si como ratos imundos... ⟪k:20⟫foi a gota d'água."

#: search2:search2_96C9AB6B_10E5_4F4F_B3E1_7362BC5E85DF
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: e165ed4c7564334c27acdad7012ae919ba49d5736d5242e9a4226e0673b460e1
#. default-sha256: 559d12f5bc0a4a5210a3189fc0bbf0aff59367f60a0c05b273e0d063d5300cfe
msgctxt "search2:search2_96C9AB6B_10E5_4F4F_B3E1_7362BC5E85DF"
msgid "⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫How could I ⟪k:4⟫not⟪k:5⟫ despise them?⟪k:6⟫"
msgstr "⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫Como eu poderia ⟪k:4⟫não⟪k:5⟫ desprezá-los?⟪k:6⟫"

#: search2:search2_F30E9911_97B5_4F96_A930_941C37493A57
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 9899cdddbcc6a0458f47757eec179056aa0fdecc14dd169cd6fca71454899289
#. default-sha256: b99cd16bfcc9bcb4e73eb81249050c61a2c215f00650cd1ffbd450d289bfdf64
msgctxt "search2:search2_F30E9911_97B5_4F96_A930_941C37493A57"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫I don’t believe I actually had the power to perform miracles when I was alive. ⟪k:2⟫It "
"was all faith—⟪k:3⟫the illusion of belief.⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫I was neither a saint nor a witch.⟪k:7⟫"
"⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫The blood wine was only effective because people placed their faith in the other "
"“Saintess.”⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫I was only ever human."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Não acredito que realmente tivesse o poder de fazer milagres quando estava viva. ⟪k:2⟫"
"Foi tudo fé—⟪k:3⟫a ilusão da crença.⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫Eu não era nem uma santa nem uma bruxa.⟪k:7⟫"
"⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫O vinho de sangue só foi eficaz porque as pessoas depositaram sua fé na outra "
"“Saintess.”⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫Eu sempre fui apenas humana."

#: search2:search2_B4504D02_0981_443C_B804_2831336A7ECA
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 3382181183f83acb26ffedd04c460efb9e8a9a8d146ed979ecce31ef9ec2ef2b
#. default-sha256: b32906d3f99f413b7ae8f295444fffdd9d425a61c74f4784db9e8d1ad2d7c9c1
msgctxt "search2:search2_B4504D02_0981_443C_B804_2831336A7ECA"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫And so I made my “wish.”⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫Most people might consider it a curse, but to "
"me, it was most certainly a wish. ⟪k:5⟫And my Father—or maybe the Devil—granted that wish!⟪k:6⟫"
"⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫From the garden, ⟪k:10⟫there rose a scream. ⟪k:11⟫The flaxen-haired young man knew "
"that voice better than anyone. ⟪k:12⟫He went deathly pale, darting down the spiral staircase "
"until he reached a window.⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫A young girl was on her knees, vomiting blood "
"in the grass."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫E assim eu fiz meu “desejo.”⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫A maioria das pessoas pode considerar isso "
"uma maldição, mas para mim, certamente foi um desejo. ⟪k:5⟫E meu Pai—ou talvez o Diabo—concedeu "
"esse desejo!⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫Do jardim, ⟪k:10⟫ergueu-se um grito. ⟪k:11⟫O jovem de cabelos "
"linho conhecia aquela voz melhor do que ninguém. ⟪k:12⟫Ele ficou mortalmente pálido, descendo a "
"escada em espiral até alcançar uma janela.⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫Uma jovem estava de joelhos, "
"vomitando sangue na grama."

#: search2:search2_8F9B772C_1BDB_483A_B813_8E71566AA03C
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 312d7a943cb513cae4d900a4ae7d00fff1b06de909fbc02ded3123342c1bdb3d
#. default-sha256: f1f20e431eded7e5574a4a32def4e16fc8b49faa6842e14b0c76da104582ab38
msgctxt "search2:search2_8F9B772C_1BDB_483A_B813_8E71566AA03C"
msgid "⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫“That wine you’re drinking is no medicine!”"
msgstr "⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫“Esse vinho que vocês estão bebendo não é remédio!”"

#: search2:search2_A5409E40_F807_4CF8_BCB0_0ECFA2BE964C
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 4604ca29bf6ce457275a46ab013c1f62deeb9b8af4a9aebe7cdae25a5b9a9dc5
#. default-sha256: 0538141dac5021201c1668336261a22a543a334e064a809f44108d779f8236f6
msgctxt "search2:search2_A5409E40_F807_4CF8_BCB0_0ECFA2BE964C"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫The nun was the first target of their outrage.⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫What she had claimed to be "
"medicine ⟪k:5⟫had turned out to be blood—an unclean substance. ⟪k:6⟫The blood of a witch, no less."
"⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫A servant of the Church—a servant of the Lord—had given her followers blood to "
"drink.⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫And at this, their indignation surged uncontrollably."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫A freira foi o primeiro alvo de sua indignação.⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫O que ela alegou ser "
"remédio ⟪k:5⟫acabou por ser sangue—uma substância impura. ⟪k:6⟫O sangue de uma bruxa, ainda mais."
"⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫Uma serva da Igreja—uma serva do Senhor—deu sangue a seus seguidores para beber."
"⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫E com isso, a indignação deles surgiu incontrolavelmente."

#: search2:search2_210C09EE_BB41_4179_8290_604B318B65B6
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: bd8e8c875a98b09d1b71d9dd20c5c41096a32c00706521bac2085e71341cb279
#. default-sha256: 01380767ac87504f3f5139551909ee4ea68a1dcd35da782be5fc5ae41ec69004
msgctxt "search2:search2_210C09EE_BB41_4179_8290_604B318B65B6"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫The people surrounded her, tying her up and throwing her to the ground. ⟪k:2⟫As they "
"prepared to inflict righteous justice upon her, the swordsman soared down the stairs and into the "
"garden, plunging his blade into anyone standing near the nun.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫The cries of agony "
"ringing through the church grounds were ear-splitting. ⟪k:6⟫It was no longer a place of God—but "
"Hell on Earth. ⟪k:7⟫Hell built up by the hands of man. ⟪k:8⟫Hell painted red with the blood of "
"their brothers."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫As pessoas a cercaram, amarrando-a e jogando-a no chão. ⟪k:2⟫Enquanto eles se "
"preparavam para infligir legitima justiça sobre ela, o espadachim desceu as escadas e foi para o "
"jardim, mergulhando sua lâmina em qualquer um que estivesse perto da freira.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫Os "
"gritos de agonia ecoando pelo terreno da igreja foram ensurdecedores. ⟪k:6⟫Não era mais um lugar "
"de Deus—mas o Inferno na Terra. ⟪k:7⟫Inferno construído pelas mãos do homem. ⟪k:8⟫Inferno pintado "
"de vermelho com o sangue de seus irmãos."

#: search2:search2_B507AAEE_793D_4CF3_B5C2_995B9F14FBB4
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 53835cd803014b96a7245b2399a5894b2279669a80d09059a8a25feacd226f6d
#. default-sha256: ee04cca1bcaa171b20d000a22af4a8a76979e5e290d67ddaa7330b96344fffd0
msgctxt "search2:search2_B507AAEE_793D_4CF3_B5C2_995B9F14FBB4"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫The people armed themselves with anything they could find and went after the man. ⟪k:2⟫"
"As much of a beast as he may have been, ⟪k:3⟫he stood little chance against such numbers.⟪k:4⟫"
"⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫It is the fate of a beast to be exterminated by those he terrorizes. ⟪k:8⟫And once "
"he was gone, the nun had no one left to protect her. ⟪k:9⟫She too was consumed by their frenzy."
"⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫All that remained was an inextinguishable inferno.⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫Hysteria "
"and despair.⟪k:16⟫⟪k:17⟫⟪k:18⟫Madness and outrage—⟪k:19⟫and no outlet for it.⟪k:20⟫⟪k:21⟫⟪k:22⟫It "
"was a revolt that made the slaves’ uprising at the lord’s manor look like a game."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫As pessoas se armaram com tudo o que conseguiram encontrar e foram atrás do homem. ⟪k:2⟫"
"Por mais besta que ele possa ter sido, ⟪k:3⟫ele teve poucas chances contra tais números.⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫"
"⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫É o destino de uma besta ser exterminada por aqueles que ela aterroriza. ⟪k:8⟫E uma vez "
"que ele se foi, a freira não tinha mais ninguém para protegê-la. ⟪k:9⟫Ela também foi consumida "
"pelo frenesi deles.⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫Tudo o que restou foi um inferno inextinguível.⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫"
"⟪k:15⟫Histeria e desespero.⟪k:16⟫⟪k:17⟫⟪k:18⟫Loucura e ultraje—⟪k:19⟫e nenhum local de escape "
"para isso.⟪k:20⟫⟪k:21⟫⟪k:22⟫Foi uma revolta que fez a rebelião dos escravos no feudo senhorial "
"parecer uma brincadeira."

#: search2:search2_C7935711_6F4C_4DFD_BC3B_ECE822B612EE
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: ba974b27ee77a0e795a1e42b7991190cabe21457c1d2c4797999ee1f77ebec45
#. default-sha256: f0220410c9d79ea5636c68bb9cbd11cd346bcf21753d0be8f1beeeca48339fa5
msgctxt "search2:search2_C7935711_6F4C_4DFD_BC3B_ECE822B612EE"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Eventually, their rage found a new target—the lord. ⟪k:2⟫It was only natural, for he "
"⟪k:3⟫was⟪k:4⟫ the true villain.⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫He was the one who had given money—and the witch’s "
"blood—to the church. ⟪k:8⟫He was the one who had profited off it.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫And above all, "
"people often resented those who stood above them. ⟪k:12⟫Particularly in times of unrest.⟪k:13⟫"
"⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫The city resounded with cries for the lord’s head."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Eventualmente, sua raiva encontrou um novo alvo—o lorde. ⟪k:2⟫Era natural, pois ele "
"⟪k:3⟫era⟪k:4⟫ o verdadeiro vilão.⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫Fora ele quem dera dinheiro—e o sangue da bruxa—"
"para a igreja. ⟪k:8⟫Foi ele quem lucrou com isso.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫E, acima de tudo, as pessoas "
"frequentemente se ressentem daqueles que estão acima delas. ⟪k:12⟫Particularmente em tempos de "
"agitação.⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫A cidade ressoou com gritos pela cabeça do lorde."

#: search2:search2_53D2C993_3E8B_407C_BE57_8430F4D6FC62
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: bde6d4d3fc48a7958565bb3e165e88138da87577541c4ee118cef9f1c5ca8cd5
#. default-sha256: db0e3dddd9e608510fc8043f6be7df9c399f14ca9e78eaf527d62300aa56638e
msgctxt "search2:search2_53D2C993_3E8B_407C_BE57_8430F4D6FC62"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫With that, the raging furor mostly settled down, but it was hardly the end of the "
"destruction. ⟪k:2⟫Mere days later, a plague befell the city.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫Dreadful black spots "
"covered the flesh of the infected. ⟪k:6⟫They writhed in pain, screaming and vomiting blood. ⟪k:7⟫"
"Ghastly howls echoed through the streets—as though the whole city had been possessed. ⟪k:8⟫It "
"became a cursed land.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫In their diseased haze, the people muttered again and "
"again,"
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Com isso, o furor em sua maioria diminuiu, mas dificilmente foi o fim da destruição. "
"⟪k:2⟫Poucos dias depois, uma praga se abateu sobre a cidade.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫Terríveis manchas "
"pretas cobriram a carne dos infectados. ⟪k:6⟫Eles se contorciam de dor, gritando e vomitando "
"sangue. ⟪k:7⟫Uivos medonhos ecoaram pelas ruas—como se toda a cidade tivesse sido possuída. ⟪k:8⟫"
"Tornou-se uma terra amaldiçoada.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫Em sua confusão doentia, as pessoas "
"murmuravam de novo e de novo,"

#: search2:search2_90684BFF_2F0D_4D0B_B5EB_E8F9CFD38C09
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 336d50c67296fe8d80a2c9ebc3132dcf2556f2521ea1defb9b415b4d63ae0cec
#. default-sha256: f493a2d9ee73a2569939ccfc58561a6ae1a2b9f6da470772d11e48430a9718f2
msgctxt "search2:search2_90684BFF_2F0D_4D0B_B5EB_E8F9CFD38C09"
msgid "⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫“We have been cursed by the witch!”"
msgstr "⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫“Nós fomos amaldiçoados pela bruxa!”"

#: search2:search2_96CB9713_8876_46E6_8C86_85EB9C18DB5F
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: e5aed886863bbe323186ad7a2226d1ac0a527f4e510c4856de75d322a51b592a
#. default-sha256: 97d81845fdf5666015e11c4fd12dd8f5d638d0dab21fcacd3ebf21fb93f3305c
msgctxt "search2:search2_96CB9713_8876_46E6_8C86_85EB9C18DB5F"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫My body was left abandoned at the top of the observation tower.⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫And as if "
"to seal the curse away, in their final days, the people shuttered all the windows, wrapping the "
"house in darkness."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Meu corpo foi abandonado no topo da torre de observação.⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫E como se para "
"selar a maldição, em seus últimos dias, o povo fechou todas as janelas, envolvendo as casas na "
"escuridão."

#: search2:search2_1CCF9033_B827_4EEE_A611_24DFE73697F1
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 74ec1d83d119205d9128153c7233b28e9019c54a92763aa5295143343a7a4a46
#. default-sha256: f43c6a40b48585ab1b2ae92653df4ddec2f792c6f775db91aa5371f7d73e3808
msgctxt "search2:search2_1CCF9033_B827_4EEE_A611_24DFE73697F1"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫But I wish to believe it ⟪k:2⟫was⟪k:3⟫ a miracle.⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫That even if my blood "
"didn’t have healing properties, ⟪k:7⟫and even if I wasn’t a saint, ⟪k:8⟫my wish—my curse—⟪k:9⟫was "
"what caused that uprising.⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫That ⟪k:13⟫that⟪k:14⟫ was my miracle.⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫"
"⟪k:17⟫Granted to me by God—or the Devil.⟪k:18⟫⟪k:19⟫⟪k:20⟫I choose to believe that.⟪k:21⟫⟪k:22⟫"
"⟪k:23⟫And that my miracle took on its true form thereafter."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Mas eu quero acreditar que ⟪k:2⟫foi⟪k:3⟫ um milagre.⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫Que mesmo que meu "
"sangue não tivesse propriedades curativas, ⟪k:7⟫e mesmo que eu não fosse uma santa, ⟪k:8⟫meu "
"desejo—minha maldição—⟪k:9⟫foi o que causou aquela revolta.⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫Que ⟪k:13⟫isso⟪k:14⟫ "
"foi meu milagre.⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫⟪k:17⟫Concedido a mim por Deus—ou pelo Diabo.⟪k:18⟫⟪k:19⟫⟪k:20⟫Eu "
